---
source: crates/rumps-query/tests/scripts.rs
description: "; Test: indentation-based expression continuation\n; Expressions continue across newlines when indented\n\n; === Basic continuation ===\n\nLET x = 1\n    + 2\nOUTPUT x\n; Expected: 3\n\nLET y = 10\n    - 3\n    - 2\nOUTPUT y\n; Expected: 5\n\n; === Multi-operator continuation ===\n\nLET sum = 1\n    + 2\n    + 3\n    + 4\nOUTPUT sum\n; Expected: 10\n\n; === Mixed operators with precedence ===\n\nLET expr = 1\n    + 2\n    * 3\nOUTPUT expr\n; Expected: 7 (1 + (2 * 3))\n\nLET expr2 = 2\n    * 3\n    + 4\nOUTPUT expr2\n; Expected: 10 ((2 * 3) + 4)\n\n; === Comparison continuation ===\n\nLET cmp = 10\n    > 5\nOUTPUT cmp\n; Expected: true\n\n; === Logical continuation ===\n\nLET logic = TRUE\n    AND TRUE\n    AND FALSE\nOUTPUT logic\n; Expected: false\n\n; === String concat continuation ===\n\nLET msg = \"Hello\"\n    ++ \" \"\n    ++ \"World\"\nOUTPUT msg\n; Expected: Hello World\n\n; === Continuation does NOT apply inside delimiters ===\n\n; Arrays can have newlines freely\nLET arr = [\n    1,\n    2,\n    3\n]\nOUTPUT arr[0]\n; Expected: 1\n\n; Objects can have newlines freely\nLET obj = {\n    a: 1,\n    b: 2\n}\nOUTPUT obj.a\n; Expected: 1\n\n; Blocks use braces, not indentation\nLET blk = {\n    LET inner = 5\n    inner * 2\n}\nOUTPUT blk\n; Expected: 10\n\n; === Continuation ends at dedent ===\n\nLET a = 1\n    + 2\nLET b = 3\nOUTPUT a + b\n; Expected: 6\n\nOUTPUT \"Indent continuation test complete\"\n"
---
3
5
10
7
10
TRUE
FALSE
Hello World
1
1
10
6
Indent continuation test complete
